    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "Link colour: Gradient (the default), on pinned positions",
      "description": "`Gradient` is the family default. Under a **fixed** layout the node positions are known before ECharts lays the graph out, so each edge gets a real source-to-target blend oriented along the edge. The positions come from `custom.fixedX` / `custom.fixedY` overrides — one per node, which is only addressable because a node is a field.\n\nUnder force or circular it degrades to the source node's colour: a bounding-box gradient cannot be oriented without the positions, and half the edges would report their direction backwards. The arrowheads carry the direction there instead.",
